ate a New Business Application Project. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: T2506a\n\n--- Record 605 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP HANA Development Tooling\nDescription: In the SAP HANA Native Application dev space for SAP Business Application Studio, the Dependency Viewer now allows you to perform the following new actions:    Expand or collapse all schemas in the dependency graph  Locate and focus on objects with the predictive search box    See View Database Objects with the Database Explorer. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: T2506a\n\n--- Record 606 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP HANA Development Tooling\nDescription: In the SAP HANA Native Application dev space for SAP Business Application Studio, the Explain Plan option in the SQL Console now shows data from both EXPLAIN_PLAN_TABLE and EXPLAIN_CALL_PLANS, providing a more complete view for SELECT statements that internally call procedures or calculation views.  See Use the SQL Console for SAP HANA to Query the Database. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: T2506a\n\n--- Record 607 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP HANA Development Tooling\nDescription: In the SAP HANA Native Application dev space for SAP Build Code, you can now generate realistic sample data for existing database tables using Generative AI.  See Generate Sample Data for Tables Using Generative AI. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2